It is a part of Oracle shared library.
On my system this file is located:
/<ORACLE HOME>/lib/libclntsh.so.1.0
or exactly:
/oracle/app/oracle/product/7.3.2/lib/libclntsh.so.1.0

Your trouble can be solved this way:

1) Check if you correctly define all oracle environment variables

	PATH=<...............>
	ORACLE_HOME=<...........>;           export ORACLE_HOME
	ORA_NLS=$ORACLE_HOME/ocommon/nls/admin/data; export ORA_NLS
	ORACLE_SID=<.................>;                     export ORACLE_SID

2) See for all required Oracle components are instaled.

For details refer to Oracle Instalation Guide for Digital UNIX  

-------
Good luck			andriy@trgz.lviv.ua
