Digital Fortran 90 V4.1-270
   Ladebug Debugger Version 4.0-25
   Fortran flages: -ladebug -g


Currently, I am trying to debug a program using "decladebug" but it 
failes to evaluate array expression.

According to the man page on f90, -ladebug flag enables DECladebug to 
print and assign to dynamics array using standard Fortran syntax,
including array sections but when I try to evaluate an array, I get
following error message:

   (ladebug) print rho(i,j,k)
   Symbol rho undefined.
   Error: Evaluation of 'rho' failed.
   Could not evaluate array expression rho(i, j, k).
   Error: no value for rho(i, j, k)
   (ladebug)

By the way rho is a dynamically allocated array and defined in a module
which can be share among subroutines.

Thanks in advance.

