I'm told that the problem of not being able to examine ALLOCATABLE arrays
in modules is corrected in a newer version of DECladebug.  This ships as
part of the operating system, so you might want to look for a newer
DIGITAL UNIX update.  4.0D is the current version.  The compiler is at
version 5.1, by the way.
