Greetings.

I am currently writing some software that will eventually compile
on most of the major UNIX platforms. I am having a problem with
the umount command. In the OSF header file it shows the prototype
as:

        extern int umount( char *, int );

whereas in my Linux header file it is:

        extern int umount __P ((__const char* __specialfile));

What is the second argument value in the OSF call? Thanks in
advance.


Steve



