mattias.falk@prevas.se wrote:
> 
> I have made a major screw-up. I did make copies of the original
> library files, but that doesn't help me if I can't even boot up
> the system.
>   Could anyone tell me how I should have installed the library
> files and above all how I can get the machine to boot?
> (I tried to insert the installation CD for Digital UNIX, but the
> machine didn't even try to boot from CD. I should also mention that
> I get a login prompt, but I'm not able to login. Also, the following
> error message is continously presented on screen:
> getty: cannot open "/dev/lat/624". errno: 6
> 
> I'm running Digital UNIX 4.0 on an Alpha Station.

Any Alpha boots from SRM console. The boot can be automatic if the SRMC
environment variable auto_action is set to BOOT (yours is). If you want
to stop the automatic boot you should pres <Ctrl>+<C> in the first few
seconds of the boot proces (after it gives those status info and says
"booting...")

On Alpha servers there is also a HALT switch, press it in and it won't
boot.

Now, when youre on SRM console, identify your CD-ROM (sh dev) and boot
from it (boot dka500, for instance).

Good luck.

Nix.




